openstack-neutron — OpenStack Networking (Neutron) 29.0.0 (2026.2 Hibiscus)
==============================================================================

This package installs the Neutron network service: API, RPC server and
the OVS-path agents (openvswitch, dhcp, l3, metadata). It installs
software ONLY: nothing is enabled, started, migrated or credentialed
at install time.

What it ships
-------------

  /usr/bin/neutron-*              API/agent CLIs and daemons
  neutron.wsgi.api:application    the supported WSGI application
  neutron/db/migration/alembic_migrations/   migration scripts
  /etc/neutron/api-paste.ini      upstream paste pipeline (wiring)
  /etc/neutron/rootwrap.conf + rootwrap.d/   agent privilege policy
  /etc/neutron/plugins/ml2/ml2_conf.ini      ML2 sample wiring
  /etc/init.d/neutron-*           OpenRC services (6 daemons)
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/neutron-*.service  systemd services (6 daemons)
  /etc/conf.d/neutron-api         WSGI container runtime settings (api)

Operator steps (NOT performed by this package)
----------------------------------------------

1. Write /etc/neutron/neutron.conf plus the ML2 and agent configs
   (ml2_conf.ini, openvswitch/dhcp/l3/metadata agent inis) from the
   samples and the generator inputs in /usr/share/neutron/:

     oslo-config-generator \
       --config-file /usr/share/neutron/oslo-config-generator/*.conf \
       ...
   # edit: database, keystone auth, ML2 mechanism_drivers=openvswitch,
   # tenant_network_types, OVS integration bridge, ... No database
   # driver is installed by this package: add python-pymysql for
   # MariaDB, or use sqlite for trials.

2. Initialise the database:

     neutron-db-manage upgrade heads

3. Register the service and endpoints in Keystone (operator-chosen),
   create provider/external networks and the OVS integration bridge.

4. Enable per node role, explicitly. Network/controller example:

     rc-update add neutron-api default && rc-service neutron-api start
     rc-update add neutron-rpc-server default && ...
     rc-update add neutron-dhcp-agent default && ...
     rc-update add neutron-l3-agent default && ...
   Hypervisor-adjacent (compute + network) nodes also run:

     rc-update add neutron-openvswitch-agent default && ...
   (systemd: systemctl enable --now neutron-<daemon> instead.)

Scope notes
-----------

  * ML2/OVS only. The openvswitch daemons (ovsdb-server,
    ovs-vswitchd) must be installed and running; agents reach them
    through ovs-vsctl/OVSDB. OVN is not packaged and not claimed.
  * Agents run as the neutron user and escalate per-command through
    neutron-rootwrap with the shipped filter policy; they never run
    as root.
  * Legacy VRRP HA needs keepalived (not packaged): plain routing
    and DVR are unaffected.
  * neutron-dhcp-agent spawns dnsmasq instances itself; the system
    dnsmasq service must stay off those ports.

Independence
------------

Neutron depends on the native python closure, gunicorn, OVS/dnsmasq/
iproute2/iptables/ipset/conntrack userlands and database client
libraries. It does not depend on Nova, Cinder, Glance or Horizon, and
it can be installed on its own.
